<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02347</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4129eeb6-9cca-4cc0-bea4-92e73afd0e74</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>

<para>For questions 1 - 5, the standard form of an equation is \(ax^2+bx+c\). For each expression, find the missing constant \(c\) that would make the expression a perfect square.</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−6x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 9</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+2x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+14x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 49</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−4x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 4</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+24x+ \underline{\;\;c\;\;}\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 144</para>


<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>If \(x^2−6x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to include the sign.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>If \(x^2+2x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to include the sign.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> +1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>If \(x^2+14x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to enter the sign.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> +7</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>If \(x^2−4x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to enter the sign.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -2</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>If \(x^2+24x+c\) is factored to be \((x \_\_\_\_\_)^2\), what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression? Remember to enter the sign.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> +12</para>
<para>For each equation in questions 11 - 14, use the following scenario.</para>
  
<blockquote>
  <para>Jada looks at Mai's work and is confused. She doesn't see how Mai got her answer.</para>
  <para>Complete Mai's missing steps by answering the questions to help Jada see how Mai solved the equation.</para> 
</blockquote>

<para>\(x^2+12x=13\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - </emphasis>\(x^2\;+\;12x\; +\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\) \(=\;13\;+\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> \((x+6)^2=49\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 - </emphasis>\(\sqrt{(x+6)^2}=\sqrt{49}\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> \(x+6= \pm\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 5 - </emphasis>\(x+6=\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 6 -</emphasis> \(x\;+\;6=\) \(-\) \(\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
<para>\(x=1\) or \(x=-13\)</para>


<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">
  <item>What is the missing term in Step 1?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 36</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="12" type="enumerated">
  <item>What is the missing term in Steps 4, 5, and 6?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 7</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="13" type="enumerated">
  <item>What is the value of \(x\) in Step 5?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="14" type="enumerated">
  <item>What is the value of \(x\) in Step 6?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -13</para>
<para>For questions 15 - 20, solve choose the equivalent equation with a perfect square on one side.</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="15" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+8x=2\) </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item> \((x−7)^2=54\) </item>
    <item> \((x+5)^2=12\) </item>
    <item> \((x−10)^2=91\) </item>
    <item> \((x+4)^2=18\) </item>
    <item> \((x+1)^2=1\) </item>
    <item> \((x+2)^2=9\) </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x+4)^2=18\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="16" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+10x=-13\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item> \((x−7)^2=54\) </item>
    <item> \((x+5)^2=12\)</item>
    <item> \((x−10)^2=91\) </item>
    <item> \((x+4)^2=18\)</item>
    <item> \((x+1)^2=1\)</item>
    <item> \((x+2)^2=9\)</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x+5)^2=12\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="17" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−14x=5\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item> \((x−7)^2=54\)</item>
    <item> \((x+5)^2=12\)</item>
    <item> \((x−10)^2=91\)</item>
    <item> \((x+4)^2=18\)</item>
    <item> \((x+1)^2=1\)</item>
    <item> \((x+2)^2=9\)</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x−7)^2=54\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="18" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+2x=0\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item>\((x−7)^2=54\) </item>
    <item> \((x+5)^2=12\) </item>
    <item> \((x−10)^2=91\)</item>
    <item> \((x+4)^2=18\)</item>
    <item> \((x+1)^2=1\)</item>
    <item> \((x+2)^2=9\)</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x+1)^2=1\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="19" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+4x−5=0\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item> \((x−7)^2=54\)</item>
    <item> \((x+5)^2=12\)</item>
    <item> \((x−10)^2=91\)</item>
    <item> \((x+4)^2=18\)</item>
    <item> \((x+1)^2=1\)</item>
    <item>\((x+2)^2=9\)</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x+2)^2=9\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="20" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−20x=-9\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item>\((x−7)^2=54\)</item>
    <item> \((x+5)^2=12\)</item>
    <item> \((x−10)^2=91\)</item>
    <item> \((x+4)^2=18\)</item>
    <item> \((x+1)^2=1\)</item>
    <item> \((x+2)^2=9\)</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x−10)^2=91\)</para>
<para>Solve each equation by completing the square, then choose the <emphasis>two</emphasis> roots.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="21" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−6x+5=12\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item> \(x = -1\) </item>
    <item>\( x = 5\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 2\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 7\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 6\) </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x =-1\), \(x = 7\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="22" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−2x=8\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item>\(x = 9\) </item>
    <item> \(x = -2\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 8\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 3\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 4\) </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x= -2\), \(x = 4\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="23" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(11=x^2+4x−1\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item> \(x = 14\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 110\) </item>
    <item> \(x = -6\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 2\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 4\) </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = -6\), \(x = 2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="24" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the equation \(x^2−18x+60=-21\) by completing the square.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <list>
    <item> \(x = -21\) </item>
    <item>\(x = 9\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 39\) </item>
    <item> \(x = 78\) </item>
    <item> \(x = -39\) </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = 9\)</para></section>
